00:23:15.470 --> 00:23:33.170
<v Ira Glass>Coming up, love stories between a kid and someone who is not a kid, and a duck and someone who is not a duck. And Jeanne Darst and someone who is not Jeanne Darst. That is in a minute, from Chicago Public Radio and Public Radio International, when our program continues.
<v Ira Glass>接下来，关于一个孩子和不是孩子的人，以及一只鸭子和不是鸭子的人之间的爱情故事。还有珍妮·达斯特和不是珍妮·达斯特的人。稍后为您播出，来自芝加哥公共广播电台和国际公共广播电台，我们的节目继续进行。

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:47.880
<v Ira Glass>It's This American Life. I'm Ira Glass. Today on our program, for Valentine's Day, What I Did For Love. Stories about people who believe in love and do all kinds of things for love. We have arrived at Act Two of our program. Act Two, 21 Chump Street.
<v Ira Glass>这是《美国生活》。我是艾拉·格拉斯。今天在我们的节目中，为了情人节，谈谈“我为爱所做的一切”。关于那些相信爱情并为爱做各种事情的人的故事。我们现在来到节目的第二幕。第二幕，“21号傻瓜街”。

00:23:47.880 --> 00:24:19.210
<v Ira Glass>Last year, at three high schools in Palm Beach County, Florida, a bunch of young police officers were sent undercover to pose as students. These were recent graduates of the police cadet program. And they blended right in. They went to classes. They ate in the cafeteria. The hung out on the basketball court during recess. They had fake Facebook accounts, of course. They even took the state's standardized test, the FCAT. Police officers were there undercover because parents and principals had complained about drugs being sold at the schools. Only the principals at the schools knew of their presence. No teachers knew it, no parents knew it.
<v Ira Glass>去年，在佛罗里达州棕榈滩县的三所高中，一群年轻的警官被派往卧底，装作学生。这些人是警校应届毕业生。他们融入得非常好。他们去上课，在食堂吃饭，休息时间在篮球场闲逛。当然，他们有假的Facebook账号。他们甚至参加了州的标准测试，FCAT。警察在那里卧底，是因为家长和校长投诉学校里有人卖毒品。只有学校的校长知道他们的存在。没有老师知道，没有家长知道。

00:24:19.210 --> 00:24:31.590
<v Ira Glass>Now, maybe it is hard to imagine a love story coming out of this situation, but one did. A love story where somebody went out of his way and took action at a key moment for love. Robbie Brown tells what happened.
<v Ira Glass>现在，也许很难想象在这种情况下会产生一个爱情故事，但确实发生了一个。一个有人为了爱，在关键时刻挺身而出、采取行动的爱情故事。罗比·布朗讲述了发生的事情。

00:24:31.590 --> 00:24:43.380
<v Robbie Brown>The plan was called Operation D Minus. And one of the schools included in the plan was Park Vista Community High School, where a kid named Justin Laboy, an 18-year-old honor roll student, was in the last semester of his senior year.
<v Robbie Brown>这个计划被称为“D减行动”。该计划包括的学校之一是公园景观社区高中，一名叫贾斯汀·拉博伊的学生，一名18岁的荣誉生，正在他高中的最后一个学期。

00:24:43.380 --> 00:24:50.940
<v Robbie Brown>And Justin could hardly believe his luck when a very pretty new girl-- everyone had noticed her-- showed up in not just one, but two of his classes.
<v Robbie Brown>当一个非常漂亮的新女孩——大家都注意到了她——不仅出现在他的一门课上，还出现在了两门课上时，贾斯汀简直不敢相信自己的运气。

00:24:50.940 --> 00:25:09.870
<v Justin>The name that she used was Naomi. I think it was Naomi Rodriguez. And she sat in front of me, but then I sat next to her. So I started talking to her. Oh, hey, my name is Justin, you know. Oh, I'm Naomi. I'm from New York, this and that. Oh, really? Me too. And I had a hat that said New York on it too, because I was trying to show her that I wasn't lying or faking it.
<v Justin>她用的名字是娜奥米。我想是娜奥米·罗德里格斯。她坐在我前面，但后来我坐在了她旁边。所以我开始跟她搭话：“哦，嘿，我叫贾斯汀。”“哦，我是娜奥米。我来自纽约，诸如此类。”“哦，真的吗？我也是。”而且我戴的帽子上写着纽约，因为我想向她证明我没有撒谎或伪装。

00:25:09.870 --> 00:25:22.650
<v Justin>She said she was from Queens. I'm from the Bronx. And she was Puerto Rican and Dominican. And that's what caught me even more. I was like, oh, man. OK. And I was Puerto Rican. And I was talking to her a little Spanish. She talked to me in a little Spanish.
<v Justin>她说她来自皇后区。我来自布朗克斯。她是波多黎各人和多米尼加人。这就是最吸引我的地方。我心想：“哦，天哪。好吧。”而且我也是波多黎各人。我跟她说了点西班牙语，她也用西班牙语跟我交谈。

00:25:22.650 --> 00:25:33.640
<v Justin>And then I just got really close to her. I got attached real quick. I was like, wow, look at this.
<v Justin>然后我就和她变得很亲近。我很快就迷上了她。我想：“哇，看看这个。”

