<v Robbie Brown>What did she look like?
<v Robbie Brown>她长什么样？

00:25:35.940 --> 00:26:11.460
<v Justin>She was about 5' 4", black straight hair, light-skinned. She was mature body-wise, so that caught a lot of people's attention. But the things that she did that I thought made her a real student was that she would sleep in class. She wouldn't do her homework. I would have to wake her up all the time, be like, hey, listen, wake up. You're going to get in trouble. Hey, oh, you didn't do your homework? OK, I'll let you copy my homework.
<v Justin>她大约5英尺4英寸，黑色直发，皮肤白皙。她的身材发育得很成熟，这吸引了很多人的注意。但她做的一些事情让我觉得她是真正的学生，那就是她会在课上睡觉。她不做作业。我总是不得不叫醒她，说：“嘿，听着，醒醒。你会惹麻烦的。嘿，哦，你没做作业？好吧，我让你抄我的作业。”

00:26:11.460 --> 00:26:29.940
<v Justin>Because, I mean, I take my classes seriously. But with her, it was different. I was just like, oh, man, you know? Wow, you know, she's cute. I could talk to her. I'd get in trouble once in a while. It would be like, Justin, stop talking. OK.
<v Justin>因为，我的意思是，我对课程很认真。但对她，情况不同。我就想：“哦，伙计，你知道吗？哇，你知道，她很可爱。我可以跟她聊天。”我会偶尔惹点麻烦。就像：“贾斯汀，别说话。”“好的。”

00:26:29.940 --> 00:26:40.030
<v Robbie Brown>Justin's a good-looking guy, popular and well-liked. He'd had girlfriends before but nothing that lasted. Nothing that seemed worth holding on to. But Naomi seemed different.
<v Robbie Brown>贾斯汀是个长相帅气、受欢迎且人缘很好的小伙子。他以前有过女朋友，但都没有维持太久。没有什么是值得坚持的。但娜奥米似乎与众不同。

00:26:40.030 --> 00:26:45.530
<v Robbie Brown>She was a good listener. She didn't seem to gossip or play games. She seemed very adult.
<v Robbie Brown>她是一个很好的倾听者。她似乎不爱说长道短，也不爱耍花招。她看起来非常成熟。

00:26:45.530 --> 00:27:08.420
<v Justin>It's the maturity level that I really cared for. I told her a lot of my feelings. I told her how I felt for her. I mean, I'm not the type of person to open up to you unless we have a really good relationship. And I was just opened up so much. I told her about my whole life story, about my parents. I told her problems I had.
<v Justin>我真正看重的是她的成熟度。我告诉了她很多我的感受。我告诉了她我对她的感觉。我的意思是，除非我们有非常好的关系，否则我不是那种会向人敞开心扉的人。但我敞开得太多了。我告诉了她我整个人生的故事，关于我的父母。我告诉了她我遇到的问题。

00:27:08.420 --> 00:27:14.780
<v Robbie Brown>What was it about her that made you trust her? That made you feel like you could open up to her?
<v Robbie Brown>她身上有什么特质让你信任她？让你觉得你可以向她敞开心扉？

00:27:14.780 --> 00:27:32.320
<v Justin>She had told me that she came up here with her mother. That they was having problems in New York, so they came over here to Florida to settle down, to have a better life. And little stuff like that, telling people, I believed that, oh, wow. OK, since you're telling me stuff like this, then I can tell you about my life.
<v Justin>她告诉我她和妈妈搬到这里。说她们在纽约遇到了问题，所以搬到了佛罗里达这里来安定下来，过上更好的生活。像这样的小事，告诉人们，我相信，噢，哇。好的，既然你告诉我这些事，那我也能告诉你关于我生活的事情。

00:27:32.320 --> 00:27:46.020
<v Justin>Yeah, I'm having hard troubles with this person right here. Or I'm having trouble with my parents. Little stuff like that makes people bond together.
<v Justin>是啊，我在这个人身上遇到了困难。或者我和父母之间遇到了问题。像这样的小事让人们结为一体。

00:27:46.020 --> 00:27:51.070
<v Robbie Brown>Justin believed he was seeing the signs that Naomi was starting to like him. Like him like him.
<v Robbie Brown>贾斯汀相信他看到了娜奥米开始喜欢他的迹象。那种“喜欢”他的喜欢。

00:27:51.070 --> 00:27:59.370
<v Robbie Brown>They walked together in the halls. They would text during class. He says she even let him kiss her on the cheek. And he serenaded her in front of their entire class.
<v Robbie Brown>他们在走廊里一起走。他们会在课堂上发短信。他说她甚至让他亲吻她的脸颊。他在全班同学面前为她唱了小夜曲。

00:27:59.370 --> 00:28:13.700
<v Justin>I'd be like, oh, I'm going to sing you a song. She'd be like, oh, OK. And then I'd just start singing. And then I'll get all blushed up. And be like, oh, man, what am I doing? OK, let me continue. I'll start rapping to her, and then I started singing. And I mean, I even danced too. So I danced for her and I--
<v Justin>我会说：“哦，我要为你唱首歌。”她说：“哦，好的。”然后我就开始唱。接着我脸红了。我想：“哦，天哪，我在做什么？好吧，让我继续。”我开始对着她唱说唱，然后又开始唱歌。我的意思是，我甚至还跳舞了。所以我为她跳舞，然后我——

00:28:13.700 --> 00:28:14.990
<v Robbie Brown>You really liked this girl.
<v Robbie Brown>你真的很喜欢这个女孩。

00:28:14.990 --> 00:28:23.650
<v Justin>Man, it tore me apart. I was like, oh my god.
<v Justin>伙计，那让我心碎。我当时想：“哦，天哪。”

00:28:23.650 --> 00:28:26.070
<v Robbie Brown>So you felt like all the signs were good?
<v Robbie Brown>所以你觉得所有的迹象都是好的？

